        <div class="row">
               
                <div class="col-sm-12">
                    
                    <p><strong>Providing Goods and Services to People with Disabilities <br></strong></p>
<p><strong>The Cardy Group </strong>is committed to excellence in serving all customers including people with disabilities.</p>
<p><strong>Assistive devices</strong></p>
<p>We will ensure that our staff are trained and familiar with various assistive devices.</p>
<p><strong>Communication</strong></p>
<p>We will communicate with people with disabilities in ways that take into account their disability.</p>
<p><strong>Service animals</strong></p>
<p>We welcome people with disabilities and their service animals. Service animals are allowed on the parts of our premises that are open to the public.</p>
<p><strong>Support persons</strong></p>
<p>A person with a disability who is accompanied by a support person will be allowed to have that person accompany them on our premises.</p>
<p><strong>Training</strong></p>
<p><strong>The Cardy Group </strong>will provide training to employees, who deal with the public or other third parties on our behalf. This training will be provided to new staff upon the time of hiring.</p>
<p><strong>Notice of temporary disruption</strong></p>
<p>In the event of a planned or unexpected disruption to services or facilities for clients/vendors with disabilities, <strong>The Cardy Group</strong> will notify clients/vendors promptly. This posted notice will include information about the reason for the disruption, its anticipated length of time, and a description of alternative facilities or services, if available.</p>
<p><strong>Feedback process</strong></p>
<p>Any person wishing to provide feedback on the way <strong>The Cardy Group</strong> provides goods and services to people with disabilities can provide feedback by emailing TCG at <a href="mailto:info@thecardygroup.com">info@thecardygroup.com</a>.</p>

                </div>
                
            </div>


        


